      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes `:nvidia: (H200 MIG 18GB) Multimodal Processor Shard 4`, which fails on main since 2026-10-14 (builds 94688, 94697 and later) at `test_model_tensor_schema[baidu/Unlimited-OCR]`. The `baidu/Unlimited-OCR` hub repo renamed its `model_type`, and vLLM only knew the old spelling.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `baidu/Unlimited-OCR` resolves to `UnlimitedOCRConfig` again with `trust_remote_code=False`, on both the latest hub revision and the previous one.\n- Users serving the current checkpoint no longer hit \"contains custom code ... pass `trust_remote_code=True`\".\n- No behavior change for other models.\n\n## Validation\n\nReproduced on current main, then verified with this change. Hub revisions: `8249d20b28` (latest, `model_type: unlimited_ocr`) and `07dea832e2` (previous, `model_type: unlimited-ocr`).\n\n| | `get_config(\"baidu/Unlimited-OCR\", trust_remote_code=False)` on `8249d20b28` | `...` on `07dea832e2` |\n|---|---|---|\n| main | `ValueError: ... contains custom code ...` | OK |\n| this PR | OK (`UnlimitedOCRConfig`, `model_type=unlimited_ocr`) | OK (`model_type=unlimited-ocr`) |\n\n```\npytest tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_tensor_schema.py -k Unlimited\n```\n\n- main: `1 failed` (the CI failure).\n- this PR: `1 passed`.\n\n`ModelConfig(\"baidu/Unlimited-OCR\", trust_remote_code=False, dtype=\"auto\")` also succeeds on both revisions with this change.\n\n## Details\n\nThe hub commit \"Update files for compatibility with transformers (#13)\" (2026-10-14 06:17 UTC) changed `config.json` `model_type` from `unlimited-ocr` to `unlimited_ocr`. `_CONFIG_REGISTRY` only had the hyphenated key, so the config fell through to the checkpoint's `auto_map` remote code, which `ModelConfig` rejects without `trust_remote_code`.\n\nThe change registers the underscore spelling next to the hyphenated one in the three places keyed on this `model_type`: `_CONFIG_REGISTRY`, `_MODEL_TYPES_WITH_INCORRECT_TOKENIZER_CLASS` and `_MODEL_TYPE_TO_CHAT_TEMPLATE_FALLBACK`. `_register_config_class` sets `config_class.model_type` to the key it registers, so one class serves both spellings. The hyphenated keys stay so older revisions and local copies keep loading.\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR touches this (searched open PRs for `Unlimited-OCR`, `UnlimitedOCR`, `test_tensor_schema`). The alternative of setting `trust_remote_code=True` in `tests/models/registry.py` would hide the failure in the test but leave `vllm serve baidu/Unlimited-OCR` broken for users, and would execute hub code for a natively supported model.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
